WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.350
Unit 2 is the three places.

2
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:05.307
The data platform book's
chapter on where sequel

3
00:00:05.307 --> 00:00:08.238
server touches A D C S
names three dependencies.

4
00:00:08.238 --> 00:00:12.538
First, the T L S certificate,
which encrypts client connections.

5
00:00:12.538 --> 00:00:15.959
Entra-authenticated connections
are always encrypted,

6
00:00:15.959 --> 00:00:18.725
so the Entra target depends
on it more, not less.

7
00:00:18.725 --> 00:00:21.537
Second, certificate-mapped type C logins.

8
00:00:21.537 --> 00:00:25.301
They carry permissions for signed
modules and can't be used to connect,

9
00:00:25.301 --> 00:00:29.713
and certificates of the same kind secure
Service Broker and mirroring endpoints.

10
00:00:29.713 --> 00:00:32.465
So treating type C logins
as connection logins,

11
00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:35.925
and moving them to Entra logins,
is effort they never needed.

12
00:00:35.925 --> 00:00:38.125
Third, certificate-based sign-in.

13
00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:41.184
It's the program's interim
posture for connections that

14
00:00:41.184 --> 00:00:44.575
can't reach Entra authentication
but can negotiate Kerberos.

15
00:00:44.575 --> 00:00:47.594
And it usually depends on
A D C S through the domain

16
00:00:47.594 --> 00:00:51.290
controllers' certificates, rather
than through the piv card.
